e of a scholar than a fighter, and would rather try to talk things down than fight. The sword gets really impatient with this approach.<br /> <br /> Primordial avatar: Templar Knight who only hears from his avatar when alone in prayer in a holy place like an alter. It manifests itself as a heavenly voice in his mind telling him it is the Knight's duty to place judgement down on those he meets.<br /> <br /> Questing avatar: This mage lost her parents to a Verbena group in what she thought was a ritual sacrifice. Her avatar manifests as her mothers voice calling her, guiding her towards discovering the truth.<br /> <br /> Dynamic avatar: Got a Film Noir detective archetype mage who's avatar manifests via sudden music, shapes in the smoke of his cigarette, objects falling out of his pockets, or simple that killer intuition.<br /> <br /> Dynamic avatar: Virtual Adept who isn't all that aware of his avatar, but it still manifests, sometimes as glowing icons on his computer, sometimes as a low hum, a series of beeps, or even an open window on his computer. I might also make Clippy jump out and ask if he'd like some kind of advise. &quot;It looks like you're hacking into the Technocracy's secret files. Would you like help?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, including your one, I think we've got a total of 7 so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-23-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","ti